      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment explains a long series of logical steps to justify that this is correct, but IIUC it\u0027s pretty simple: if the backend uses texture views for doing multiplanar operations, then of course the backend supports texture views.\n\nI also don\u0027t think the check is quite correct (which is _why_ it requires so much justification) - in principle, couldn\u0027t you have a multiplanar texture that doesn\u0027t use texture views, on a backend that doesn\u0027t support texture views, in which case this check would be incorrect?\n\nIf I\u0027m understanding correctly, I would phrase this like so:\n\n```\n// If the backend uses texture views for multiplanar textures,\n// we should skip this check. See https://crbug.com/382071071\nif (texture-\u003eIsMultiPlanarUsingViews() \u0026\u0026 !device-\u003eIsCompatibilityMode()) {\n```\n\nThis seems a little more complex because it introduces a new method, but I think it\u0027s more correct and self-explanatory.",
      "revId": "e9529004c6e48900ebfe1eacf18b2edc9dfdcd05",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
